        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 78-year-old male patient, admitted on 01/07/2021 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received patient education regarding inhaler technique and self-management. He responded well to treatment with satisfactory improvement in respiratory function. He is discharged in stable condition and I recommend close follow-up, optimisation of inhaler therapy, and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
